{"labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "", "image": "engenn11le06ob07re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "Thought-Oriented Roles</br></br><ul><li> To \"plant\" something means to place a seed in the ground so that it will grow into something wonderful, like a tree or flower. People who are \"plants\" have ideas about how things could be improved in the future. It has been suggested that they are motivated by praise and have difficulty dealing with criticism. Often introverted, it is observed that they prefer to work alone. Since their ideas are novel, they may be considered counter-productive at times. They may not appear to be effective communicators insofar as they tend to ignore traditional constraints.", "id": 1, "time": "10", "image": "engenn11le06ob07re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<ul><li> Monitor-Evaluators are known to be good at analyzing in that they evaluate the initiatives that plants or other people come up with. It is said that they are wise and equitable. It is believed that they always assess the advantages and disadvantages of an option before making a decision. They are often seen as unemotional or detached inasmuch as they tend to think critically and strategically. However, it is agreed upon that they are not effective motivators in that they are always reacting to situations rather than instigating change.", "id": 2, "time": "36000", "image": "engenn11le06ob07re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<ul><li> Specialists have developed valuable skills and abilities over a period of time. It is assumed that they are proud of their contribution or knowledge of the team. They work hard to maintain their professional status. They are usually introverts and lack interest 