ns or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "criticism", "type": "name"}, {"content": "remarks that say what you think is bad about someone or something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They find it hard to deal with criticism. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about team oriented roles. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "novel", "type": "name"}, {"content": "different, unique, unusual", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think their ideas are novel.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "counter-productive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having an \u200beffect that is \u200bopposite to the one \u200bintended or \u200bwanted", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Since their ideas are novel, they may be considered counter-productive at times.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "parameter", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a set of fixed limits that control the way that something should be done", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They may be a poor communicator insofar as they tend to ignore given parameters.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "constraint", "type": "name"}, {"content": "rule or regulation that limits your range of action", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They may not appear to be effective communicators insofar as they tend to ignore traditional contraints.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "detached", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not reacting to or becoming involved in something in an emotional way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They are often seen as unemotional or detached.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to instigate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make something start", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They are always reacting to situations rather than instigating change.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob07aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "territorial", "type": "name"}, {"content": "careful to guard what you consider to be your own, and prevent others from using it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They may come across as territorial.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob07aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "at the expense of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "if you do one thing at the expense of another, doing the first thing \u200bharms the second thing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They tend to be preoccupied with small details at the expense of the bigger picture.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le06ob07aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Report Verbs with Impersonal Passive Constructions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use two different patterns with report verbs: Active and Passive.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Active: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">They say </span>that it rains a lot in London</span>. <br/> Passive: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It is said </span>that it rains a lot in London</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can also use: <span class=\"italic\">It + passive report verb + finite clause</span> (a clause which can stand alone).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It is thought</span> that the Pyramids took 25 years to build.</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It is known </span>that smoking is not good for health. </span><br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It is believed</span> that there is life after death. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This pattern is often used in formal reports, news reports and academic writing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These are the verbs you can use with this structure: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It has been <span class=\"strong\">suggested </span>that they thrive on praise and find it hard to deal with criticism.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It is <span class=\"strong\">observed </span>that they prefer to work apart from the team. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It is <span class=\"strong\">believed </span>that they carefully weigh the pros and cons before coming to a decision.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"allege\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"intend\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"report\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"announce\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"know\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"reveal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"believe\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"mention\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"say\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"claim\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"notice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"see\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"consider\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"object\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"show\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"declare\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"observe\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"state\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"explain\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"promise\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"suggest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"feel\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"prove\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"recommend\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"understand\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Reason Clauses Using <span class=\"italic\">in that, insofar as, inasmuch as, since</span> and <span class=\"italic\">as</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You introduce reason clauses with specific linking words. Each linking word or phrase carries its own meaning and use.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">since </span>and <span class=\"strong\">as</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">since </span></span>and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">as </span></span>to introduce information you are already aware of.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Since </span>you've already completed your work, we can go for lunch. </span> <br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">As </span>you're new here, you should introduce yourself to everyone first.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">in that</span>, <span class=\"strong\">insofar as</span>,<span class=\"strong\"> inasmuch as</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">in that</span></span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">insofar </span></span>as and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">inasmuch as </span></span>to justify what we have just said by indicating that the statement is true. You use these words in fairly formal English. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">She's a pleasure to work for, <span class=\"strong\">in that</span> she is attentive and motivating.</span> <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">We are expecting a busy week <span class=\"strong\">insofar as</span> all the appointments have been booked.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">The employees are tired <span class=\"strong\">inasmuch as</span> they cannot work overtime.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Since their ideas are novel, they may be considered counter-productive at times. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "As they are fully committed to their field of expertise, they may come across as territorial. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Monitor-Evaluators are known to be good at analyzing in that they evaluate ideas.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They may be a poor communicator insofar as they tend to ignore given parameters and constraints. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They are critical thinkers and very strategic inasmuch as they are often perceived as detached.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Work in pairs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a summary chart of all the team roles presented by Belbin.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In your chart include all nine role names, their positive contributions, and their allowable weaknesses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Display the charts around the class and explain your chart.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I collaborate with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I analyze all the positive contributions and weaknesses of each role.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a summary chart that is interesting, easy to understand and informative.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}